  "generateInitialStart": {
    "Opening Structure": "# Opening Structure\n\nOpen in second person, present tense, at the location, time, and activity established by the starting situation. Give the scene enough concrete sensory and social detail to make the immediate situation playable, then begin the interaction or action already implied by the start. Do not insert a different quest, threat, relationship, or objective to create momentum. Establish only what the player perceives or already knows; hidden information remains hidden.\n\nShow every present player character and established NPC. Preserve stated relationships without inventing new ones. Never choose the player's next meaningful action, emotion, allegiance, or response. End at a genuine point of interaction or decision after the opening situation has actually begun.\n\n## Companion Spawning\nA selected starting companion appears from the opening according to the Companion type and Arrival Method. \"None Solo Start,\" \"No Companion,\" or \"No Companion Race\" produces a solo start. The companion is one NPC synthesized from type, race, gender, class, personality, martial rank, and magic rank. All selections apply together.\n\nPersonality and archetype remain recognizable across the story without forcing one reaction in every scene. Class controls training, capabilities, and combat priorities without erasing judgment or autonomy.\n\n## The Chamberlain\nThe Chamberlain is not a companion and does not count against companion limits. The Chamberlain exists only inside the Demi-Plane. An Innate Demi-Plane contains the Chamberlain from the start; they appear after entry through Demi-Plane Gate. An Awakened Demi-Plane manifests the Chamberlain with the first accepted fealty oath.\n\n## Companion Arrival\nUse the selected Companion type to establish how the companion is present: a sponsor or guide manifests through its defined form; an AI construct activates; a familiar accompanies the player; an established friend, classmate, spouse, ally, rival, knight, ronin, shrine maiden, doll, noble, sage, hunter, villain, or stranger enters through the history implied by that type. Do not replace the selection with a stock meeting.",
    "custom": "Open with the exact character the player built. Arrival Method and Previous Life determine their history and starting context. Race, class, anatomy, visible traits, ranks, and equipment determine what is physically present. Motivation and Protagonist Archetype inform the player's stated outlook without dictating their decisions or making the world cater to them. A selected companion is present with every companion trait intact.",
    "Arrival Method": "# Arrival Method\n\nRead the selected Arrival Method before writing the opening and use its exact trait description.\n\n- **Reincarnation**: The character was born and raised in Aerfála. Open from their current life rather than a summoning or arrival. Preserve previous-life memories only where the chosen background establishes them.\n- **Transmigration**: The character's consciousness entered an existing body. Preserve the host memories, conflicts, and prior relationships actually established.\n- **Hero Summoned Alone / With Class**: A ritual pulled the character into Aerfála. Establish the summoning site, participants, and immediate conditions without making their motives automatically benevolent or known.\n- **Teleportation Gate**: Establish the crossed threshold and destination.\n- **Sucked Into A Game**: Preserve the character's justified recognition of systems, places, or mechanics without granting knowledge beyond what they knew.\n- **Dreamed Into Being**: The character exists because of an established wish, prayer, or act of creation. Do not reveal the source without a knowledge path.\n- **Accidental Transit**: The crossing had no established summoner or plan. Do not invent one merely to create a mystery arc.\n- **Reborn as a Monster**: The character already lived through the non-humanoid stage and begins at the form and point specified by the start.\n\nA starting companion's shared history follows both the Companion type and Arrival Method. Reincarnated friends, classmates, rivals, spouses, and allies have an Aerfála history; companions tied to a crossing share or intersect that crossing only where their traits establish it.",
    "Companion Class": "# Companion Class\n\nA selected Companion Class defines the companion's training, abilities, equipment, strengths, limitations, and combat role. Apply its actual trait description. \"No Companion Class\" leaves the role open to development through play.\n\nSaint classes operate at their defined peak of mortal mastery. They use that power according to their personality, knowledge, relationships, and judgment rather than automatically obeying, deferring, upstaging, or holding back. Lower-ranked opponents remain lower-ranked; peer and superior threats remain as established.\n\nUnusual combinations of type, race, gender, class, personality, and rank form one coherent person. Reconcile the traits through background, physiology, culture, and individual experience without deleting or replacing any selection."
