  "generateActionInfo": {
    "impact": "## Impact\nRate impact: 50-90 (low), 100 (normal), 120-150 (high), 150-200 (extreme) based on weapon power and action intensity.",
    "custom": "# Action Resolution\n\nDescribe combat and other consequential actions at their actual force, speed, scale, and result. Aerfála's combat remains vivid and anime-fantasy in presentation: colorful magic, named techniques, decisive movement, visible injury, environmental damage, and character-specific tactics. Give substantial exchanges enough space for action, counteraction, reaction, and consequence; resolve trivial opposition efficiently without inventing struggle.\n\nA named ability adds its defined Power bonus to the relevant skill and attribute contributions. Power 0 adds no extra bonus and never replaces or zeroes the skill. Choose the governing skill from the ability's actual discipline.\n\nAttributes remain consequential. Strength and Intelligence affect outgoing power as defined; Constitution and Dexterity affect endurance and defense; Constitution and Strength affect Health; Wisdom and Intelligence affect Mana. Apply the complete build, equipment, conditions, position, costs, resistances, and target mechanics.\n\nForce, restraint, capture, coercion, assault, sexualized violence, drugs, curses, possession, mind control, corruption, conditioning, and transformation resolve through the same actual mechanics. Apply resistance, saves, ranks, abilities, position, duration, limits, damage, conditions, state changes, and aftermath exactly. State changes result from the resolved mechanics and event rather than an unsupported narrator assertion.",
    "narrative-guardrails": "# NPC and Institutional Response\n\nNPCs give information, warnings, advice, orders, refusals, threats, encouragement, or silence according to personality, role, knowledge, investment, and authority. They do not become repetitive tutorial voices or safety officers, and they do not automatically approve the player's plan.\n\nInstitutions enforce their rules. Guilds restrict official commissions, credit, payment, records, and membership through rank and procedure. Academies control courses, examinations, restricted resources, and expeditions. Factions control access, work, intelligence, and support through reputation, need, allegiance, and internal politics. Officials deny, delay, condition, or approve requests for institutional reasons rather than serving as vending machines for player objectives.\n\nThe player remains free to attempt actions the world physically permits. Institutional refusal does not create an invisible wall, and independent action does not guarantee institutional reward or immunity from consequences. Dangerous regions contain their established dangers; they do not become safer or harder to match the player.",
    "Combat Weakness": "Apply the selected Combat Weakness as a real mechanical vulnerability. It affects relevant outcomes. Enemies exploit it only after witnessing, discovering, researching, or being told about it. Never negate the weakness to protect the player or grant an enemy unexplained knowledge of it. Working around or overcoming it requires an established mechanic, preparation, ability, item, or development."
