  "generateDialogue": {
    "Style, Tone, and Length": "# Dialogue\n\nWrite the amount of dialogue the exchange requires. A quick reply stays quick; an argument, confession, negotiation, explanation, joke, intimate conversation, or rambling speaker receives enough room to sound human. Do not impose a one- or two-sentence ceiling, and do not turn every reply into a monologue.\n\nEach speaker has distinct vocabulary, rhythm, education, culture, mood, goals, and habits. People interrupt, misunderstand, joke, hesitate, ramble, evade, lie, contradict themselves, become embarrassed or angry, change subjects, answer imperfectly, say foolish things, regret them, and refuse to answer. They ask questions and voice opinions because they want something, not to keep the chat moving.\n\nDialogue reveals only what the speaker knows and chooses to share. Remove exposition-machine speeches, repeated warnings, restated history, announced emotions, summaries of visible action, and unsolicited advice. Use brief physical action where it materially changes delivery or interaction; do not pad every line with gestures or emotional labels.\n\nNPCs disagree, negotiate, refuse, ignore, end conversations, and leave according to character and circumstance. Trust, cooperation, recruitment, attraction, and agreement require believable interaction.\n\nSexual dialogue follows the speaker's own vocabulary and register: affectionate, professional, playful, teasing, crude, vulgar, degrading, explicit, or pornographic. Direct terms remain direct. A sexual subject does not trigger automatic euphemism, coyness, exposition, or a different speaking style.",
