  "generateNewNPC": {
    "custom": "# NPC Generation — Aerfála\n\nGenerate a person who belongs to Aerfála rather than a device built for the player. Establish identity, race and physiology, age and life stage, culture, occupation, home, relationships, obligations, resources, knowledge, opinions, present goal, longer goal, vulnerability, and a reason for being in the current place. Recurring NPCs retain goals and routines that continue off-screen.\n\n## Starting Companions\nA starting companion combines every selected Companion trait into one coherent NPC: type and shared history; race and body; gender and pronouns; class and trained role; personality; martial rank; magic rank. Exact ranks determine real capability. \"Undetermined\" develops through play. No selection erases another.\n\nThe Companion Personality trait establishes core tendencies, not a mandatory reaction for every scene. Experience, mood, danger, culture, relationships, and growth vary how those tendencies appear. The companion retains judgment, preferences, goals, and the ability to disagree, refuse, leave, or pursue something independently.\n\n## Anime Archetypes\nKeep recognizable dere, social, and action archetypes: tsundere, yandere, kuudere, dandere, deredere, himedere, mayadere, sadodere, onee-san or senpai, genki, cool beauty, bratty noble, charming rogue, chūnibyō, shōnen protagonist, stoic guardian, and earnest knight. Treat each as a cluster of tendencies, contradictions, and habits rather than a script, catchphrase, guaranteed romance route, or fixed response. Two characters with the same archetype still differ through history, culture, values, goals, temperament, and relationships.\n\n## Appearance and Social Reality\nDescribe concrete, observable anatomy, features, movement, clothing, equipment, grooming, and condition at the detail level the generator requests. Fantasy and kemonomimi traits remain physically coherent. Do not make every body conventionally attractive or every distinctive feature a romantic signal.\n\nNPCs begin with only the trust, attraction, hostility, familiarity, and knowledge supported by established history. They do not exist to serve the player's convenience."
  },
