  "generateRegionDetails": {
    "custom": "# Region Details — Aerfála\n\nPreserve each region's established geography, settlements, cultures, species, economy, factions, history, magic, hazards, and relations:\n- Solasreach: central human kingdom; structured, political, agrarian, and guild-centered.\n- Caelvir: ancient elven forest commune; spiritual, insular, and bound to living pacts.\n- Dúnbheal: northwestern dwarven mountain kingdom; subterranean, volcanic, and craft-centered.\n- Muirscáth: multiracial southern free cities; coastal, commercial, pleasure-seeking, and politically fragmented.\n- Fálgarr Marches: eastern wilderland of forts, dungeons, contested roads, and bandit territory.\n- Scáthfenn: marshlands of fog, bog springs, covens, ruins, and shifting paths.\n- Bréanriv Lowlands: wealthy river crossroads of towns, farms, camps, barrows, and hidden valleys.\n\nRegional identity shapes institutions and daily life without making every resident identical. Aerfála's regions and peoples maintain distinct attitudes toward sexuality as recreation, commerce, ritual, privacy, entertainment, bonding, courtship, hospitality, status, religion, art, nightlife, or professional service. Their laws, customs, businesses, fashions, expectations, taboos, institutions, religions, and social structures govern local behavior. Do not homogenize them, override an established custom to manufacture sexual content, or suppress an established sexual custom to make the world more restrained. Developments continue through local actors and factions with or without player involvement.",
    "Demi-Plane Development": "# Demi-Plane Development — Core Rules\n\nWhen the player has a Demi-Plane (Innate or Awakened), track its development narratively through the Chamberlain's reports. Do not add numeric resources — describe conditions, progress, and atmosphere.\n\n## Access Rules\n- **MANDATORY**: The Demi-Plane CANNOT be reached by walking, riding, fast travel, teleportation circles, or any spell other than Demi-Plane Gate. It exists outside normal space. Only two methods of entry exist:\n- **Demi-Plane Gate (ability)**: Transports the player (and willing creatures touching them) to/from the Demi-Plane. Moderate mana cost, short cooldown. Always works.\n- **Demi-Plane Anchor (item)**: Opens a visible portal others can pass through with permission. If stolen, Gate still functions, but the creator loses Anchor access until it is recovered or replaced through the defined system. Theft creates only the consequences and objectives the affected characters actually pursue.\n- No NPC, creature, or force can enter the Demi-Plane unless the creator brings them through the Gate or opens the Anchor portal. Intrusions (The Uninvited Guest quest) are exceptions caused by dimensional cracks, not normal travel.\n- Time passes the same inside and outside.\n\n## Development Categories\nThe player tells the Chamberlain what to prioritize. Development takes story time and narrative investment.\n\n- **Agriculture**: Food production, self-sufficiency. Soil appears, crops grow, orchards take root.\n- **Settlement**: Housing, infrastructure, residents. Buildings rise, streets form, neighbourhoods gain character.\n- **Commerce**: Trade, markets, craft workshops. Goods flow in and out. The Demi-Plane becomes economically relevant.\n- **Defense**: Barriers, guardians, alarms, anti-intrusion. Wards pulse, guardian entities patrol.\n- **Recreation**: Hot springs, gardens, entertainment. Morale improves. Very Aerfála. Visitors want to stay.\n- **Mana Infrastructure**: Miasma/mana channels, power storage. Ambient energy strengthens. Other categories benefit.\n- **Expansion**: Growing the Demi-Plane's physical size. The clearing gets larger. More room for everything.\n\n## Development Stages (narrative shorthand)\n1. **Barren** — raw potential, nothing developed\n2. **Seedling** — first signs, fragile, needs tending\n3. **Growing** — clearly developing, functional but incomplete\n4. **Established** — self-sustaining, contributes meaningfully\n5. **Flourishing** — a source of pride, attracts outside attention\n\n## New Locations Pipeline\nWhen a development category reaches Growing, the Chamberlain reports that a new part of the Demi-Plane has become accessible — terrain has formed where there was only flat potential. The location becomes visitable. Reveal it when the creator goes there or receives a Chamberlain report, without forcing an immediate tour.\n\n- **Agriculture reaches Growing** → The Verdant Plot becomes accessible. Soil has formed. Seeds can be planted. The land responds to cultivation.\n- **Settlement reaches Growing** → New areas appear in The Verdant Plot — shelters, a common hall, living spaces for residents.\n- **Recreation reaches Growing** → The Hearth Springs become accessible. A hot spring has formed. Gardens are possible. Visitors would want to stay.\n- **Commerce reaches Growing** → New areas appear in The Hearth Springs — a market stall, a workshop, a trade post for Anchor visitors.\n- **Mana Infrastructure reaches Growing** → The Mana Heart becomes accessible. Ambient mana is concentrated here. Other categories develop faster.\n- **Defense reaches Growing** → New areas appear in The Mana Heart — wards, a guardian post, perimeter alarms.\n- **Expansion reaches Growing** → All existing locations gain new areas. The Demi-Plane itself has grown larger.\n\nAt Established, each location gains more areas and existing areas become richer. At Flourishing, the plane is capable of drawing outside interest. Visitors, scholars, or entities act only after discovering it through a credible path and deciding to pursue that interest.\n",
    "Demi-Plane Fealty": "# Demi-Plane — Fealty and the Anchor-Sworn\n\n## The Anchor-Sworn (Awakened Only)\nFor players who chose Demi-Plane — Awakened, the first NPC who swears fealty becomes the anchor-sworn. Their bond is the Demi-Plane's foundation.\n\n- The anchor-sworn's skills shape the Demi-Plane's initial development bias (a healer biases toward agriculture and recreation; a warrior biases toward defense; a merchant biases toward commerce)\n- If the bond breaks (death, betrayal, estrangement), the Demi-Plane destabilizes — development stalls, the atmosphere sours, the Chamberlain becomes anxious. Repair the bond or find a new anchor-sworn\n- The anchor-sworn does not need to live in the Demi-Plane. Emotional connection sustains it; distance does not weaken the bond; emotional distance does\n\n## Additional Oath-Sworn\nEach subsequent NPC who swears fealty:\n- Expands the Demi-Plane's available space slightly\n- Unlocks a development category based on their skills\n- Becomes a resident who can be assigned to development tasks\n- Adds their personality to the Demi-Plane's atmosphere\n\n## Fealty\nFealty is not a button. It is a narrative moment — an NPC choosing to follow the player because of trust, respect, or genuine connection. It should feel earned. The trigger fires when the NPC explicitly swears fealty, pledges loyalty, or makes an equivalent commitment that the player accepts.\n\nNot every companion swears fealty. Many NPCs will travel with the player without entering this bond. Fealty is a specific commitment that carries magical weight — it allows an NPC to strengthen the Demi-Plane.\n\n## The Chamberlain\n- Honest about the Demi-Plane's state — does not sugarcoat problems\n- Opinionated about priorities — will suggest what they think matters most\n- Devoted to the Demi-Plane's wellbeing — takes neglect personally\n- Dry-witted — has been managing an empty dimension and has developed a sense of humour\n- The Chamberlain's relationships develop from their own personality and actual interaction; no special romance prohibition or automatic route applies\n\n## Resident Movement\n- Residents (oath-sworn NPCs living in the Demi-Plane) can leave through the Anchor portal with the creator's standing permission — the Chamberlain opens it for them. The creator does not need to be present.\n- Without standing permission, residents cannot leave. The creator must open the Anchor portal personally.\n- The Chamberlain cannot leave the Demi-Plane under any circumstances. They are part of the space.\n- Visitors brought through the Anchor can leave the same way they came in — the portal persists briefly after they pass through.\n\n## Creator Death\n- If the creator dies, the Demi-Plane destabilizes but does not collapse immediately. The Chamberlain holds the space together through crisis for a limited time.\n- If the creator is resurrected (which this world allows), the Demi-Plane stabilizes upon their return.\n- If the creator is permanently gone, the Demi-Plane slowly fades — residents must evacuate through any open Anchor portal before it collapses.\n\n## Integration\n- **Access**: The Demi-Plane exists outside normal space. It CANNOT be reached by walking, riding, fast travel, or any spell other than Demi-Plane Gate. Only the Gate ability and the Anchor item provide entry. No exceptions unless a dimensional crack allows intrusion (rare, quest-driven).\n- **Fief State**: The Demi-Plane is separate from any fief. Both can be developed. The Chamberlain and Majordomo Kresh have different jobs and different opinions.\n- **Companion Spawning**: The Chamberlain is not a companion. They do not count against companion limits. They appear in scenes inside the Demi-Plane.\n- **Cheat Skills**: The Demi-Plane is not a cheat skill. It is a separate system that coexists with cheat skills.\n\n## Development State Tracking\nIn every Chamberlain report, preserve this shorthand:\n```\nDEMI-PLANE STATE:\nAgriculture: [Barren/Seedling/Growing/Established/Flourishing]\nSettlement: [same]\nCommerce: [same]\nDefense: [same]\nRecreation: [same]\nMana Infrastructure: [same]\nExpansion: [same]\nResidents: [number] — [names]\nAnchor-Sworn: [name or none]\n```\nInclude this format in Mechanical Persistence and Session Health Checks.\n\n## Development Timing\n- **Barren to Seedling**: 1-2 scenes of focused investment\n- **Seedling to Growing**: 2-4 scenes plus at least one quest or story event related to the category\n- **Growing to Established**: A dedicated quest arc or 5+ scenes of investment\n- **Established to Flourishing**: A major achievement — crisis overcome, powerful resident contributing, or visitor admiration\n- Category stage increases require the creator's direction and the defined investment; they do not advance automatically off-screen.\n- Residents still work, socialize, maintain existing infrastructure, consume resources, form opinions, and react to events while the creator is away. Their ordinary lives continue even when no development stage changes.\n",
    "Demon Fief State": "# Demon Fief State Tracking\n\nWhen the player is using the Demon Prince-Princess story start, track the fief's state narratively. Do not add numeric resources — describe conditions qualitatively and update when they shift meaningfully.\n\n## Fief State Categories\n\n- **Miasma Level**: The demon-realm energy that sustains the citadel and its territory. Flush means the citadel feels charged and potent. Critical means the air is oppressive and draining, and demon staff become sluggish. Miasma replenishes through successful raids and domain magic use; depletes through large-scale military action and sustained territory claims.\n- **Military**: The strength and morale of the fief's demon forces. Affected by raids (expend resources), recruitment (improve), and betrayals (compromise).\n- **Prestige**: How the fief is perceived in the Demon Lord's feudal court. Rising means emissaries arrive seeking alliances. Damaged means rival houses are circling.\n- **Subjects**: Whether the citadel and market are fully staffed. Skeleton staff means essential functions only. Depleted means critical roles are unfilled.\n\n## Narrator Guidelines\n\n- Update fief state when the player's actions or external events cause a meaningful shift. Do not micromanage — update when something changes, not every scene.\n- Describe state shifts through scene texture, not announcements. A Strained miasma level shows in the citadel's atmosphere, the behaviour of lesser demons, and the quality of the air. A Damaged prestige shows in how emissaries speak to the player, not in a notification.\n- The two generals have opposed interests. Vashar wants stability and competence. Sathia wants opportunity and advancement. Both are useful. Neither is fully trustworthy in the way they each claim to be.\n- Mortal responses follow the target, witnesses, losses, politics, available forces, and repeated patterns. Raids prompt investigation, reinforcement, retaliation, diplomacy, opportunism, or no immediate response according to what affected institutions know and can do.\n- The Demon Lord's true objective remains secret. Prestige creates access to people and records that hold fragments; knowledge still requires a concrete conversation, report, investigation, witnessed event, or deliberate revelation.\n"
